+## Optional QML parser
+
+`tree-sitter-qmljs@0.3.1` is an optional dependency. On hosts without a compatible native build (including native Windows), npm may omit it. The first QML load failure emits one notice per process; concurrent and subsequent files reuse the failed load and fall back to text chunking. QML files remain indexable, without QML AST metadata. TypeScript, JavaScript, Python, Go, Rust, Java, Bash, C and C++ keep their existing grammars. To restore QML AST support, install a working optional dependency and restart the process.
+
 ## Pi and OMP Support
 
 `pi-knowledge` supports direct Pi extension loading through `pi -e ./extension.js` and OMP-compatible loading through the same packaged entry shim. The root `extension.js` and `index.ts` stay startup-light so install-time validation can inspect the extension without resolving native runtime dependencies such as `better-sqlite3` or `onnxruntime-node`.
