+QML support uses optional `tree-sitter-qmljs@0.3.1`; it extracts structural UI metadata only. The package has no Windows prebuild; a failed install must not block other languages. Runtime import failure emits a single notice per process and is cached before awaiting so concurrent indexing does not repeat it. QML then uses text chunks. Restart after fixing the optional native binding to retry. An ambient declaration keeps TypeScript builds valid when npm omits the optional package entirely; it does not provide a runtime grammar.
 It is not a Qt semantic analyzer and does not infer runtime signal wiring or component instantiation beyond parsed file structure.
 
